d 'FVGEN': module to flatten factor-variable interactions into labeled main-effect and product variables
d
d  fvgen expands a factor-variable interaction specification, such
d as i.sex##c.age, into ordinary variables: an indicator for each
d categorical level (the base level dropped by default) and a
d product variable for each interaction term, with variable labels
d built from value labels so that a model fitted on the flattened
d variables exports as one clean, self-labeled row per coefficient.
d The flattened model is an exact reparameterization of the native
d factor-variable model. Options set per-factor reference levels
d (ref()), materialize every level, mean-center continuous terms
d before forming products, produce per-group slopes within levels
d of a variable (simple()), append the base level to main-effect
d labels, control the name prefix and the interaction label symbol,
d replace colliding variables, and drop all generated variables.
d The margins option refits the model with native factor syntax so
d that margins can be used, optionally storing the clone. Results
d returned in r() include the effective specification, the counts
d and names of main-effect, interaction, and generated variables,
d and the variables ordered for estimation. 
d
d KW: factor variables
d KW: interactions
d KW: indicator variables
d KW: dummy variables
d KW: value labels
d KW: variable labels
d KW: regression tables
d KW: export
d KW: margins
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261030
d
d Author: Timothy P Copeland, Karolinska Institutet
d Support: email timothy.copeland@@ki.se
d
f fvgen.ado
f fvgen.sthlp
